  "worked_solution": "First, notice that the domain $R$ can be represented as a union of three sub-domains, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & =S\\cup T\\cup U.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={\u222c}_{S}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{T}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{U}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{S}(\\sqrt[3]{x}y-\\sqrt[3]{y})\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{T}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{U}0\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\u222c}_{S}(\\sqrt[3]{x}y-\\sqrt[3]{y})\\,\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{T}2x{y}^{3}\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
